# The demo shop's real signed-in session — a real bearer/refresh token, regenerated by
# seed-demo-account.mjs. Same class of secret as apps/console/e2e/.session.json; never committed.
.demo-session.json

# The same shop's LOGIN — the phone and password its signup used. Kept beside the session and
# never committed for the same reason: it is a real credential. It exists because a session can
# only ever be re-minted from it — a demo account's own signup phone is random and, once lost, the
# whole account is unreachable no matter how much data it holds.
.demo-credentials.json

# The same pair for every other named demo shop (lib/demo-session.mjs's profiles — seed-demo-apps/
# uses "apps"). Same secret class, same reason.
.demo-session.*.json
.demo-credentials.*.json

# The affiliate manager's own signed-in session — seed-affiliate-team.mjs's own real bearer
# token, same class of secret as the shop's .demo-session.json above and never committed for the
# same reason. Unlike the shop, this account's phone/password are fixed constants in that script
# itself (never randomly generated), so there is no matching .demo-affiliate-credentials.json —
# nothing here can ever become unrecoverable the way a random shop signup phone could.
.demo-affiliate-session.json

# Same class of secret, for seed-demo-affiliate.mjs's marketer account instead of the shop's own.
.demo-affiliate-credentials.json

# seed-demo-apps/local_stack.py's runtime state — its venv, service logs, object store, and the
# shared secrets (PII_SALT, the token-signing secret) every local service was started with. The
# secrets are per-machine and must stay stable for the life of the local data, so they live here
# and never in git.
.local-stack/

# seed-affiliate-tools.mjs's own manager account — a THIRD affiliate demo account, deliberately
# seeded with real templates/citations/a Places key/a referred shop, unlike the earnings tour's
# deliberately-empty one and the team tour's manager-plus-promoters one. Same secret class.
.demo-affiliate-tools-session.json
